WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.220
Have you ever had your knitting fall off
the machine, get your carriage stuck,

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:10.010
or find that a stitch
pattern is just not working?

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:15.780
Even the most experienced machine knitter
has one of THOSE days, now and then.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.160
In this video,
we'll cover some of the common things

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:22.620
that can happen,
and we'll talk about how to avoid them.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.100
A lot of things can go
wrong when casting on.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.420
I can't cover all
the different cast-on methods.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:35.300
Each has their own little quirk, but there
are some general things to watch out for.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.040
If your carriage jams after you cast on,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.660
it might be that the carriage isn't
seated correctly on the needle bed.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.000
Remove it and the yarn,
replace the carriage,

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:50.180
and run it across the needle bed
with all the needles out of work.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.780
It should move smoothly and easily.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.300
Maybe your cast on is too tight.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:00.760
Remove the yarn from the needles and cast
on more loosely with the method of your

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:05.770
choice, or maybe try
a different cast on method.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.520
Check to make sure that you're using

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.570
the yarn that's the correct size
for the needles of your machine.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.080
When you're using the right yarn,

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:19.200
your carriage will move smoothly
and easily and won't jam.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.420
Maybe the yarn tension is too tight.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.280
Make sure that it's not caught up

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:29.820
in the yarn guides and check maybe
the tensioner for tangles and knots.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.660
It needs to be loose enough to feed

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:35.520
through the carriage
so it can move easily.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:42.080
If you've pulled all the needles out maybe
to do an E-wrap cast on and they don't

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:47.540
knit when you push the carriage across,
maybe you have the machine set to hold.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:53.930
Check your hold setting on your carriage,
disable the hold, and try again.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.800
Sometimes after casting on all

00:01:55.830 --> 00:02:00.260
the stitches drop or they make
large loops in a big yarn mess.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.820
Check to make sure that the yarn is

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.220
engaged in the yarn feeder
of the carriage correctly.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.640
Also, check that it's in the right feeder.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.660
Some machines have two yarn feeders.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:16.940
Another thing that can happen is that your

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.500
sinker plate is not seated
properly in the carriage.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:26.020
Remove the carriage,
reseat that sinker plate, and try again.

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:28.920
If, after casting on some stitches drop

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:34.060
at the beginning of the row,
your yarn is probably too loose.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:37.380
Try again and adjust the tensioner

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:43.220
and try taking up the slack of the yarn
at the beginning of the row.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.300
If stitches drop in the middle of the row,

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.820
probably the sinker plate
is not seated properly.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.660
Loosen the screws holding the sinker

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:56.380
plate, push them back in,
reseed it, take the whole carriage off.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.800
Make sure that the sinker plate is
attached to the carriage correctly.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:06.540
Another issue could be that yarn
is tangled in the sinker brushes.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.540
Remove your carriage, look underneath,

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:15.920
make sure there isn't any yarn or lint
stuck in those brushes.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.560
Now, if the stitches drop in the middle

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:23.060
of the row, the cast-on might
be too loose or just uneven.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:28.260
Confirm that the stitches of your
original cast-on are even.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.520
If you find that stitches are tucking or

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:33.540
they just don't knit off the needles
properly,

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:38.240
your cast on is probably too tight
or the stitch tension is way too low.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.140
Those stitches are way too tight.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:44.200
You can knit individual stitches manually

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:50.820
to fix this or take everything
off the machine and try it again.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:53.900
Sometimes the stitches just won't knit.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:04:00.610
Maybe your cast on is too loose or your
controls are not set to plain knitting.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.520
It sounds silly, but take a look and make

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:08.800
sure that the settings on your
carriage are set for plain knitting.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.760
No matter what's happening,

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.820
if you're struggling with your
cast on, check these things.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:18.280
Are you using the right
yarn for your machine?

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.020
Are the settings on your carriage correct?

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:26.220
Is the carriage seated
on the needle bed properly?

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.860
Are the sinker plate in the
carriage joined correctly?

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.960
Okay.
Check your yarn.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:38.180
Is it feeding smoothly without any knot,
or tangles, or hangups anywhere?

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.580
Is your yarn in the right
feeder of the carriage?

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.320
Is your cast on too tight, too loose?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.460
Try this.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:52.300
Try casting on with another method.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.120
You might have more success.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:59.100
Sometimes all it takes is getting up,

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:05.980
taking a deep breath, walk away, and come
back to it, and your problem is solved.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.040
Happy knitting.

